18. There is a history of severe drug allergy, including but not limited to antibody drugs and small molecule targeted drugs;
19. Known history of mental illness or drug abuse;
20. There is an unhealed wound;
21. Take it within 7 days before enrollment or expect to take it after enrollment, which is known as a strong CYP3A4/5 inhibitor and CYP3A4/5 inducer (including but not limited to carbamazepine, phenobarbital, phenytoin, rifabutin, Rifampicin and Hypericum perforatum, etc.) or drugs that may cause arrhythmia (including but not limited to terfenadine, quinidine, procainamide, disopyramide, sotalol, probucol and bep) Lee, etc.);
