Inclusion Criteria:

1. Age between 35 and 80 years, regardless of gender.
2. For patients with prior lipid-lowering treatment: screening LDL-C ≥1.8 mmol/L; for treatment-naïve patients: screening LDL-C ≥2.6 mmol/L.
3. Lp(a) ≥30 mg/dL.
4. Onset of symptoms within 3 to 7 days.
5. Diagnosis of ischemic stroke (NIHSS score ≤20) or high-risk TIA with ABCD² score ≥4; and meeting at least one of the following imaging criteria:

(1) Large-artery atherosclerosis (LAA) subtype per TOAST classification: vascular imaging confirms ≥50% atherosclerotic stenosis of the intracranial or extracranial culprit artery.

(2) Head CT or MRI demonstrates acute multiple infarcts, with etiology consistent with large-artery atherosclerosis (including nonstenotic vulnerable plaques).

6.The patient or their legally authorized representative has provided written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Have received or are planned to receive intravenous thrombolysis or endovascular thrombectomy;
2. Definite cardioembolic ischemic cerebrovascular disease, such as that associated with atrial fibrillation, prosthetic heart valves, atrial myxoma, endocarditis, etc.;
3. Ischemic cerebrovascular disease with other definite etiologies, such as aortic dissection, cervical or intracranial arterial dissection, vasculitis, vascular malformation, moyamoya disease/moyamoya syndrome, fibromuscular dysplasia, etc.;
4. Non-vascular intracranial diseases, such as intracranial tumors, multiple sclerosis, etc.;
5. Neuroimaging showing that the infarct area of the index cerebral infarction involves more than one-half of a single cerebral lobe;
6. Neuroimaging showing hemorrhagic transformation of the index cerebral infarction;
