12. History of intracranial hemorrhage, such as intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH) or subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH);
13. History of intracranial or extracranial angioplasty;
14. History of gastrointestinal bleeding or major surgery within the previous 90 days;
15. Planned surgery or interventional procedure within 90 days that may require discontinuation of the study treatment;
16. Severe organic disease with an expected survival of less than 1 year;
17. Pregnant women, or women of childbearing potential who are not using effective contraception and have no documented pregnancy test;
18. Currently participating in another clinical trial involving an investigational drug or device;
19. Unable to complete follow-up due to geographic or other reasons, such as alcohol abuse, drug abuse, dementia, or severe psychiatric disorders;
20. Use of a PCSK9 inhibitor, including monoclonal antibodies or small interfering RNA (siRNA), within the previous 6 months;
21. Thrombocytopenia (platelet count \<100 × 10⁹/L), coagulation disorders, or systemic bleeding.

